{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 30, :comments ["<b>אין, סוס</b> — [ל–לא] two joined. That is: there is no man whose wisdom, understanding, or counsel avails him against YHWH — that is, to escape His hand by any one of them — even if he prepares a horse to flee. For on a day of war there is no power to escape and to save oneself, for salvation belongs to HaShem, and He grants it to whom He wills."], :book :proverbs, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 21, :notes {0 "The bracketed [ל–לא] likely indicates that ל is joined to לא without a makaf; rendered as a note on the grammatical joining of the two words."}, :source-witnesses [["Ibn Ezra on Proverbs -- Daat" "http://www.daat.ac.il/he-il/tanach/parshanut_hamikra/full-text/eben-ezra/mishley/"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T19:24:06.520500354Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}